    q: 'Why is multiple sclerosis on a melanocortin site?',
    a: 'Because repository corticotropin, a long-acting ACTH gel, is FDA-labelled for acute exacerbations of multiple sclerosis in adults. ACTH is a melanocortin peptide cut from POMC. High-dose corticosteroids are the usual treatment for a relapse; the gel is an alternative, including when steroids have not worked.',
  },
